[[File:S1E04 Suits.png|thumb|170px|[[DeFoe]]'s Suits in the [[Cave of the Gargoyle]]]]
[[DeFoe]] had his Suits pursue [[Lok Lambert]] in an attempt to retrieve [[Eathon Lambert's journal]] and its secrets of the [[Amulet of Will]]. Three of them cornered him in the courtyard of [[Dante Vale's house]] but were defeated by [[Dante Vale]]. {{source|A Seeker Is Born}} DeFoe's Suits staked out Dante's house before chasing him and Lok through Venice. They were defeated with help from [[Sophie Casterwill]] and [[Santiago]]. Later, a large group of Suits attacked the [[Venice Huntik Library]] where they fought Dante and Santiago. In the midst of battle, however, the Huntik team were able to escape. {{Source|The Casterwill Client}} 

Pursuing the Foundation's clue regarding the [[Metagolem|Golem]], [[the Organization]] sent Suits to infiltrate and attack the [[Prague Huntik Hotel]]. After DeFoe found [[Jodis Lore's Key]], the Suits attacked the team again. However, despite gaining the upper hand, the Suits were forced to retreat when Lok arrived to turn the tables giving Dante time to recover the Amulet and summon Metagolem. {{source|Words of Truth, Heart of Lies}} 
[[File:S1E06 French Suits.png|thumb|170px|Two of DeFoe's French recruits]]
The team was later sent to [[Rouen, France]], to retrieve [[Gar-Ghoul]]. {{source|Into the River of Secrets}} However, they missed the more important information on the [[Ring of Arc]] and were then sent by [[the Professor]] to [[Paris, France]], following Dante's team into the [[Paris Catacombs]]. {{source|Crawling the Catacombs}} Despite gaining a number of new recruits from Paris, they were unsuccessful at retrieving the Ring. {{source|Divide and Conquer}}

His Suits were later sent after [[King Basilisk]], but lost the Titan to [[Zhalia Moon]]. They also lost [[unnamed Suit 001]] to a petrification trap within the Titan's chamber. {{source|Absent Heroes}} Upon this failure, DeFoe lost command of his original team of Suits and thus had to rally his remaining loyal Suits within [[Velo, Greece]], in an attempt to finally get his revenge on [[Dante Vale]]. This team failed and were escorted back under [[Grier]]. {{source|The Treasures of the Argonauts}}

[[File:S1E16 Klaus Suits.png|thumb|170px|Two of [[Klaus]]' Viennese Suits guarding his lab]]Klaus' Viennese Suits were sent, under the instructions of Rassimov, to go after [[Dante Vale]] in [[County Kerry, Ireland]]. His team of Suits ambushed [[Scarlet Byrne]] and Dante's team in the [[New Grange Passage Tomb]], using their powerful spells and Titans to gain the upper hand. However, they were eventually defeated after [[Sandra Lambert]] arrived, making a vital intervention. {{source|Home Turf}} 
[[File:S1E14 Klaus Egypt Suits.png|thumb|170px|Klaus and his Egypt Suits]]
Klaus sent his Egyptian Suits to excavate the [[tomb of Nefertiti]], and both his Suit teams were sent after the [[Sceptre of Nefertiti]], which was taken from the Foundation members after a skirmish. {{source|The Sceptre Deception}} During the mission to secure the Amulets of [[Vlad Dracul]], three of his Suits were transformed through the power of [[Overmode]]. Even with this power, however, they were defeated when [[Zhalia Moon]] chose to side with the [[Huntik Foundation]]. {{source|The Vampire Loses Its Fangs}}

[[File:S1E21 Rassimov Suits Lok.png|thumb|170px|[[Rassimov]] and his Suits face Lok in [[Atlantis]]]]
DeFoe's former Suits were placed under [[Rassimov]] and given an improved arsenal of Titans. They were then sent by Rassimov to ambush [[Lok Lambert]] and [[Sophie Casterwill]], who were working at a burger joint in [[Venice, Italy]]. The Suits were defeated by Lok and Sophie, who were joined by [[Zhalia Moon]]. {{source|All Work and No Pay}}

Two of the recruits from Paris, also formerly under DeFoe, were sent by Rassimov in an attempt to eliminate [[Sophie Casterwill]] and company. They failed to hinder the Foundation members, however. More of his Suits, who had infiltrated the [[Mausoleum of Sir Lancelot]], confronted the Foundation team but were swiftly defeated. {{source|Memory Lane}}

His Suits were then sent by [[the Professor]] to the coasts of [[Turkey]] in search for the [[Ring]] of [[Behemoth]]. Though two of his Suits were overpowering the native [[Amazons]], they were defeated by Dante, Lok, and Sophie. Rassimov later joined his team, but the Suits were defeated Dante received the Ring of Behemoth from [[Zhalia Moon]]. {{source|Ladies' Choice}}

[[File:S2E24 Suits 051 052.png|thumb|170px|[[Alpha]] and [[Beta]], the Professor's personal Elite Suits]]
The Professor and his two elite agents, [[Alpha]] and [[Beta]], travelled to [[King Solomon's Mines]] on the trail of the Ring of [[Tao]]. {{source|The Golden Asp}} After entering the Mines, the Suits fought aginst the Huntik team and [[Montehue]] and [[Tersly]]. Despite overpowering the Foundation's forces, they were forced to retreat when Lok bonded with Tao. {{source|To Be Together}} The two agents later attacked Dante's house and left the team considerably injured and worse for wear. {{source|The Secret of Two Generations}} They fought against the team at the Professor's castle but were defeated. {{source|The Divine Comedy}}

Following the Professor's defeat, the two agents attacked the Huntik team after they broke into Organization central but were defeated. {{source|Doorway to Huntik}}

Under the command of [[Wilder]] and [[Hoffman]], the two agents defended the Professor's castle from Dante and Grier before being defeated. {{source|An Ally from the Organization}}

[[File:S2E27 Suits.png|thumb|170px|Wilder's Suits attack]]
A new team of six Suits was banded together by [[Wilder|Mr. Wilder]] and sent to Peru, in order to destroy the Huntik team so that Wilder could become the new leader of the Organization. {{Source|Doorway to Huntik}} The Suits helped Wilder take over [[Tower of Nostradamus]] and take [[Peter]], [[Billie]] and [[Annette]] hostage. {{source|The Tower of Nostradamus}} Wilder's Suits travelled to [[:Category:Avalon|Avalon]] where they fought the Huntik team and [[LeBlanche]]. {{Source|Knight of the Willblade}}

When Lok and Sophie broke into the safehouse at the [[Golem's Attic]] on the [[Road of Alchemists]], the Suits arrested them and attempted to transport them back to HQ. However, they were attacked by Dante, Zhalia and [[Lucas Casterwill]]'s team, forcing them to retreat. {{Source|Chasing Void}}

When the Huntik team launched an assault in [[Klaus' bookshop|Klaus' lab]], the Suits fought against them, with one invoking a [[Redcap]] Titan, while two others lay in ambush with [[Stack]]. Later, two of them were ambushed by two [[Silent Soldiers|Silent Soilders]].{{Source|The Blood Spiral}}
[[File:S2E46 Suits Augerfrost.png|thumb|170px|Wilder's Suits attack the team at [[the Professor's castle]]]]
Two of Wilder's Suits attacked [[Sophie Casterwill]] in Hamelin, to get information about her. They overpowered her and [[Sabriel]], with their new Titans, [[Shadow Agent]] and [[Doom Warden]]. However, as one of the Suit attempted to finish Sophie off with [[Stoneblade]], [[Den Fears|Den]] and [[Cherit]] came in to save her.{{Source|Gremlow Infestation}} The Suits were waiting on motorbikes to ambush the Huntik team as they landed in [[:Category:Baja California, Mexico|Baja California]] but were stopped by Dante, Lok and Den also on motorbikes. Later, two Suits fought the team in [[Hernán Cortés' vault]], but retreated when [[Conquistador]] ran riot. {{Source|The Power of Umbra}}

Wilder's Suits fought the Huntik team once again when they, guided by [[Grier]], invaded [[The Professor's castle|The Professor's Castle]], to recover the Professor's files on [[Rassimov]]. Four of them were defeated by [[Dante Vale|Dante]] and Grier, wile the other two were defeated by [[Lok Lambert|Lok]], Den and Cherit, while trying to stop the three of them from moving forward through the castle.{{Source|An Ally from the Organization}}

{{for|specific info on each individual Suit's Spells and Titans|Suits/List of Suits}}
[[File:S1E02 Mactavish invokes Redcap 2.png|thumb|200px|[[Mr. Mactavish]] invokes [[Redcap]]]]
The Suits' greatest asset is their sheer numbers, but they also make capable spies and are excellent at gathering information. In a battle, the Suits are trained to fight with a variety of spells and Titans. Just as the Organization brings about cold, unfeeling order with the help of savage evil deeds, its troops fight with Titans such as the cold [[Mindrone]] and the savage [[Redcap]], and use the spell [[Augerfrost]] to knock their targets out cold.

[[File:S1E16 Enforcer Bonelasher Suits.jpg|thumb|The [[Bonelasher]]/[[Enforcer]] pairing favored by [[Klaus]]' Suits]]
Many Suit teams fight using a conventional two-Titan combination, matching a ground-based frontline brawler with a ranged, aerial attacker, as seen with DeFoe and Grier's teams who often paired [[Redcap]] and [[Mindrone]] together. {{Source|S1E02}} {{Source|S1E12}} Klaus' Austrian Suits also followed this convention by primarily using [[Bonelasher]] and [[Enforcer]] together. Later on, Wilder's Suits returned to this formation by often using [[Venomaster]] and [[Gigadrone]] together. {{Source|S2E27}} 

Other Suit teams do not rely on this standard combination pairing. [[Rassimov]]'s Suit team used a far more diverse range of obscure and dangerous Titans from across the Organization roster, a tactic which made them far more challenging and dangerous in combat. {{Source|S1E19}} {{Source|S1E22}} {{Source|S1E23}} More elite agents, such as [[Beta]], possess larger, more powerful Titans such as [[Terrapede]]. {{Source|S1E25}} Some Suits' Titan rosters also very by region, with many Paris agents favoring the Titan, [[Jokoul]]. {{source|Divide and Conquer}} {{Source|S1E18}} Klaus' Egypt team rely solely on multiple [[Sekhmet]] Titans along with [[Unnamed Suit 030|Suit 030]] invoking a single [[Ammit Heart-Eater]]. {{Source|S1E14}}

